// `ctxc check` checks a program as `ctxc run` and as `ctxc test` build it, at once. A
// directory of `#test` fns alone needs no `main`, as for `ctxc test`.
//# $ ctxc check {dir}/tests
//# stderr:
//| check: no errors
//# $ ctxc run {dir}/tests
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| {dir}/tests/t.ctx:1:1: error: no `fn main` entry point

// A program with a `main` and tests has both checked.
//# $ ctxc check {dir}/both
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| {dir}/both/t.ctx:6:12: error: unknown name `wrong`
//| check: 1 error; not checked until the program has no other error: the order of a call's fields, what tasks borrow, consts computed by running code

// With neither a `main` nor a test there is nothing to run.
//# $ ctxc check {dir}/neither
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| {dir}/neither/t.ctx:1:1: error: no `fn main` entry point
//| check: 1 error
